            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did the last two words of the chapter before mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: दीवार",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "दीवार (dīvār) — \"a wall\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A Persian word, dīvār, 'wall'. Its older Iranian form was a compound, and the piece at the front of it is not certainly identified, so this book will name the Persian and stop there."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is a loan and not a cousin, which is worth keeping straight: दरवाज़ा, which you already own, is Persian too, and the two of them furnish most of the outside of a Hindi house between them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five parts of the house."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
