        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: छत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "छत (chat) — \"a roof\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit छत्र (chatra), which meant a parasol — the thing held over a person's head. The word came down off the handle and settled onto the building."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A flat छत (chat) in North India is a place people go, not only a lid: it is where washing dries and where the evening is sat out. The word covers the surface and the use at once."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The second of five, and a parasol that turned into a roof."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
