          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सीढ़ी (sīṛhī) — \"a staircase, a ladder\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "सीढ़ी (sīṛhī) is traced to a Sanskrit word for a flight of steps, but the exact form behind it is disputed and the sources differ on which one it was."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The word does not distinguish a staircase from a ladder. Both are सीढ़ी (sīṛhī), because what the word names is the going up, not the thing's construction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The fourth of five, and one word for two objects."
