          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: चादर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "चादर (chādar) — \"a sheet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian chādar, a sheet or a veil — a single broad piece of cloth, whatever it is spread over. English borrowed it too, as chuddar."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So it ends the chapter the way दीवार (dīvār) began it: a Persian word for a plain domestic thing, taken whole. A Hindi house is furnished in two languages at once, and neither of them is hiding."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The fifth of five. That is the house, wall to roof."
            }
          ]
        },
